Fresh-eyes review complete on `src/blog/people/drafts/Noah-Wyle.md` — notes appended as a `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-08-09)` block at the bottom of the file, no body edits made.

The two biggest issues I flagged:

1. **His real service record is missing, and it's the piece's own thesis.** The draft closes on "he spent thirty years reporting for duty," but skips his strongest duty evidence: volunteering with Doctors of the World in Kosovo refugee camps (which directly seeded ER's Congo/Darfur storylines) and decades as artistic producer of The Blank Theatre Company in LA. The "Capitol Twice" section currently implies those two visits are the whole case file — these two facts outrank both visits.

2. **The wilderness years are a hole.** Fifteen years get compressed to "science-fiction dads and swashbuckling librarians" without naming Falling Skies or The Librarians. Readers who know him from those franchises will feel a third of his career waved off — and both shows are unused Loyalist evidence (anchoring long-run ensembles instead of chasing reinvention, which is exactly the point that section is making).

Other notes in the block: the volunteer email is leaned on five times across sections; the season 2 "intervention for a fictional doctor" clause is the most startling claim in the piece and gets half an ambiguous sentence; Pirates of Silicon Valley (the Macworld imposter story is dead on-theme and would let the body *show* his humor instead of telling it); a narrator-command tic ("Read that sentence closely," "Notice what he did," etc.) that makes the template audible; plus preserve-list items — the drawer dialogue, the "Somewhere" ending, and the Capitol two-date structure are the best material and shouldn't be touched.

Sources: [From ER to Global Humanitarian (2024 doc)](https://www.imdb.com/title/tt34913553/), [Life Stories interview](https://www.lifestories.org/podcast-items/noah-wyle-from-er-to-global-humanitarian), [About the Artists — Blank Theatre credits](https://www.abouttheartists.com/artists/326070-noah-wyle)
